<h1>CACHING</h1>
<h2 class="mt-4">Caching on anonymous requests for Products GET (Blazor Consumer, not Blazor Admin).</h2>
<h4 class="mt-2">2 Factors affect appearance of caching</h4>
<p class="mt-2">Whether the request is actually cached based on time.</p>
<p class="mt-2">Whether the page data is refreshed based on Blazor Component architecture </p>
<p>    --- Product List and Detail are child components of Storefront, so unless they are intentionally refreshed after add/update/delete, the data is not refetched when switch pages.</p>
<p>    --- This means, even with no caching, the data in the list and detail is not refreshed unless a PAGE CHANGE is commanded, or a product is ADDED, UPDATED, DELETED.</p>
<p class="mt-2">For Blazor Admin, caching is currently not used as it uses DownstreamApi, hence requests have auth header, so API will not cache response.</p>
